From 46fffc6c714098b08fbbbaae5258ac750ce6f2ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Wed, 20 May 2026 13:18:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf phase 11 patch 0164 -- Leg B audio tick-boundary pump
 (486-campaign Bug 2 continuous-SFX-stutter fix)

486-campaign Bug 2 -- continuous SFX stutter on slow CPUs during
steady-state gameplay (independent of stage-load freezes, which are
covered by 0162-v2 Leg A + 0163 data cache). Per flush-instr's
docs/internal/AUDIO-PIPELINE-CAMPAIGN-DESIGN.md sec.1.2: the
cooperative-scheduler audio thread only runs when the engine
yields, so during heavy render frames the engine can defer the
yield past the SB16 ring depth (~372 ms Tier-2), draining the ring
below underrun threshold. Once-per-frame supplementary pumping
from the render thread keeps the ring topped up across consecutive
heavy frames -- the audible stutter resolves.

Wave-38 cooperative-scheduler starvation pattern (per
wave_38_cooperative_scheduler_starvation_is_real) is the
mechanism: this patch addresses it at the render-thread side
(while patches SDL/0067-v2 + 0068 add the audio-thread-side
export + backstop the SDL/0067 path needs to be safely callable
from main).

Lever shape -- single TICKPUMP() call in run_tick_fixed:

Sentinel-cached killswitch helper `tickpump_active()` + `TICKPUMP()`
macro at file scope in src/main.cpp (mirrors 0162-v2's
midgap_pump_active / MIDGAP_PUMP idiom, which lives in map.cpp
because all 6 Leg A call sites are inside load_stage). One
TICKPUMP() call site in run_tick_fixed, placed immediately before
`game.tick_render_submit()`. Both the 1:1-mode FIXED_TIMESTEP path
(line 401 `game.tick_state()`) and the catch-up `else`-block path
(lines 405-461, with the catch-up while-loop + ftd_on diagnostic +
spiral-of-death resync) converge at this point, so the pump fires
exactly once per displayed frame regardless of FT mode.

Macro body: `do { if (tickpump_active()) while (SDL_DOSAudioPump()) { } } while (0)`.
The while-loop tops up the ring to FULL on each tick boundary;
bounded by ring depth (~372 ms Tier-2 / ~23 ms per buffer-frame ->
~16 iterations worst-case from empty, 1-2 in steady-state at 30 fps
real-HW render rate). In the silent case (no SFX, no Organya, no
MIDI) SDL_DOSAudioPump returns false on the first call and the loop
body executes zero times -- auto-degenerates to no-op at zero CPU
cost.

Killswitch: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_TICKPUMP. **v1 default OFF**
(opt-in via "=1"). Same hygiene as nxengine/0162-v2 + 0163 --
ship opt-in; flip to default-ON in a release patch after iter
validation confirms stutter elimination + no per-flip cost
regression in cells that don't need it. Sentinel-cached on first
tickpump_active() call -- single SDL_GetHint then cached int;
banner emit "audio tick-boundary pump: ENABLED (opt-in)" /
"audio tick-boundary pump: DISABLED (default)" on the decision.

Placement rationale (per the #97 STOP-and-ack):
- Line 463 (immediately before tick_render_submit), NOT line 435
  (immediately after catch-up while-close): line 435 would skip
  the 1:1-mode path entirely (line 401 bypasses the else block),
  AND would shift the spiral-of-death resync trigger boundary at
  lines 446-461 by adding pump latency before the accum_ns
  mutation. Line 463 sits after all logic-state mutation has
  stabilized and before render-submit reads drawcalls.
- The design doc's "main.cpp:~428-431" was a line-number drift
  (those lines are inside the catch-up while-body in the current
  tree); line 463 is the correct mapping of the prose intent
  ("between catch-up close and tick_render_submit").

Wave-36 trap clearance: the pump invokes SDL_DOSAudioPump() (the
SDL/0067-v2 export). It does NOT call game.tick_state, does NOT
submit drawcalls, does NOT re-enter the catch-up loop. Same safety
profile as 0162-v2's MIDGAP_PUMP. The wave-36 mechanism (-28 fps in
slot 0135 / mechanism_a_drawcall_coupling_bug) was catch-up
applied OVER game.tick (which submitted drawcalls); this is
post-catch-up, drawcall-side-effect-free.

Default-OFF byte-identical-at-rendered-frame to pre-0164:
- TICKPUMP() with active=false evaluates only the cached int
  compare per frame -- no SDL_DOSAudioPump call, no audio thread
  interaction.
- The only side-effect in the cache-OFF path is the banner
  LOG_INFO line on first call (one line per process), which
  matches the 0162-v2 / 0163 banner-only-no-state-change pattern.

Coexists with SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_MIDGAP_PUMP (independent
killswitches; Leg A covers stage-load freads, Leg B covers
steady-state tick boundaries). Both share the same SDL_DOSAudioPump
export from SDL/0067-v2 and the same SDL/0068 TryLock+timeout
backstop.

Single-lever-per-binary: the tick-boundary pump is THE
operator-visible mechanism this binary's new patch introduces.
SDL-side patches (SDL/0063+0064+0065+0066+0067-v2+0068+SDL_mixer/0001+0002)
and prior nxengine patches (...+0160+0161+0162-v2+0163-v2) are
unchanged carriers from the iter rotation. The 3-cell iter
attribution remains clean:
- PLAY0: baseline (both new killswitches unset).
- PLAY1: SET SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_TICKPUMP=1 -- Leg B only.
- PLAY2: SET SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_PRELOAD_MIDI=1 -- existing
  patches/nxengine-evo/0112+0114 MIDI parse cache only.

Files in this patch:
- src/main.cpp -- one new SDL3/SDL_dosaudio_pump.h include + one
  new helper block (~50 LOC including DOS-PORT comment) at file
  scope between ft_accumulator_thaw and run_tick_fixed + one new
  TICKPUMP() call + comment at the tick boundary (~10 LOC).

No CMakeLists.txt change needed; no new TU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/main.cpp | 60 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 60 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/main.cpp b/src/main.cpp
index 01856fb..1fca25f 100644
--- a/src/main.cpp
+++ b/src/main.cpp
@@ -42,2 +42,3 @@ extern "C" {
 #include <SDL3_image/SDL_image.h>
+#include <SDL3/SDL_dosaudio_pump.h>  // patch 0164: SDL_DOSAudioPump for the tick-boundary audio pump
 using namespace NXE::Graphics;
@@ -322,2 +323,54 @@ extern "C" void ft_accumulator_thaw(void)
 
+// DOS-PORT (patch 0164, Leg B audio tick-boundary pump -- 486-class
+// campaign Bug 2 fix for continuous SFX stutter). Sentinel-cached
+// killswitch helper + TICKPUMP macro. Mirrors nxengine/0162-v2's
+// MIDGAP_PUMP idiom (whose helper lives in map.cpp because all 6
+// Leg A call sites are inside load_stage's sub-loaders). Leg B fires
+// at the once-per-displayed-frame tick boundary instead, so the
+// helper + macro live here at file scope in main.cpp -- the single
+// TICKPUMP() call site sits in run_tick_fixed right before
+// game.tick_render_submit() (the boundary between logic-tick state
+// mutation and render-submit drawcall gather; both the 1:1-mode
+// path and the catch-up else-block path converge here, so the pump
+// fires exactly once per displayed frame).
+//
+// Killswitch: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_TICKPUMP. v1 default OFF
+// (opt-in via "=1"); same hygiene as nxengine/0162-v2 + 0163.
+// Sentinel-cached on first tickpump_active() call -- single
+// SDL_GetHint then cached int; banner emit on the decision.
+//
+// SDL_DOSAudioPump is exported from sdl-engine's SDL/0067-v2 -- a
+// thin wrapper around the SDL3-DOS backend's audio servicing path
+// (no renderer call, no SDL_PumpEvents, no engine callback path
+// beyond Pixtone scalar slot bookkeeping internal to SDL_mixer)
+// that moves one buffer-frame of audio from the bound streams into
+// the ring and returns 1 if more work could be done, 0 if the ring
+// is full or no work is queued. The while-loop tops the ring up to
+// FULL on each tick boundary; bounded by ring depth (~372 ms Tier-2
+// / ~23 ms per buffer-frame -> ~16 iterations worst-case from
+// empty; 1-2 in steady-state at 30 fps real-HW render rate). With
+// the killswitch off (the v1 default), zero pump calls execute;
+// only the cached int compare runs per frame, so the v1 default
+// path is byte-identical-at-rendered-frame to pre-0164.
+//
+// Wave-36 trap clearance: the pump does NOT call game.tick_state,
+// does NOT submit drawcalls, does NOT re-enter the catch-up loop.
+// Same safety profile as 0162-v2's MIDGAP_PUMP (which ships clean
+// at 6 sites inside load_stage). The wave-36 mechanism (-28 fps in
+// slot 0135) was catch-up applied OVER game.tick(), which submitted
+// drawcalls; this is post-catch-up, drawcall-side-effect-free.
+static int  g_tickpump_decided = -1;
+static bool tickpump_active()
+{
+  if (g_tickpump_decided < 0)
+  {
+    const char *e = SDL_GetHint("SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_TICKPUMP");
+    g_tickpump_decided = (e && e[0] == '1' && e[1] == '\0') ? 1 : 0;
+    LOG_INFO("audio tick-boundary pump: {}",
+             g_tickpump_decided ? "ENABLED (opt-in)" : "DISABLED (default)");
+  }
+  return g_tickpump_decided == 1;
+}
+#define TICKPUMP() do { if (tickpump_active()) while (SDL_DOSAudioPump()) { } } while (0)
+
 static void run_tick_fixed(void)
@@ -463,2 +516,9 @@ static void run_tick_fixed(void)
   // --- RENDER: ONCE per displayed frame ---
+  // patch 0164 (Leg B audio tick-boundary pump): top up the SB16 ring
+  // via SDL_DOSAudioPump at the tick boundary, before the render-submit
+  // gather. Fires once per displayed frame (both 1:1-mode and catch-up
+  // paths converge here); gated on tickpump_active() (default OFF). No-op
+  // when the killswitch is unset -- byte-identical-at-rendered-frame to
+  // pre-0164.
+  TICKPUMP();
   game.tick_render_submit();
-- 
